(6190, '2026-07-27 00:00:00', '2026-07-27 13:42:40', 20, '1.) SQL Injection (SQLi): Allows attackers to execute malicious SQL queries by injecting harmful input into database operations.\r\n\r\n2.) Reflected XSS: Occurs when user input is reflected in the response without proper validation, allowing script execution.\r\n\r\n3.) HTML Injection: Happens when untrusted input is inserted into HTML pages without encoding, allowing UI manipulation or fake content injection.\r\n4.) Session Cookie Issue: Same session cookie is used before and after login, increasing the risk of session hijacking.\r\n\r\n5.) Local Storage Security Issue: Sensitive data stored in browser local storage can be accessed by JavaScript, stolen via XSS, and remains unencrypted.\r\n6.) Outdated jQuery Version: Application is using an old jQuery version with known security vulnerabilities.\r\n7.) Outdated jQuery Version: Application is using an old jQuery version with known security vulnerabilities.', '10:07', '19:18', '09:11', 101),
